            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A two-digit number is randomly chosen from 10 to 99, inclusive. Define the events below. Determine if ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "A",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " and ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "B",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " are independent events.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p39-q16",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p39-q16-events",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\begin{aligned}A&=\\text{the number is divisible by 15}\\\\B&=\\text{the last digit is 5}\\end{aligned}",
                  "display": true
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Dependent events: $P(A\\cap B)=\\frac{1}{30}$, whereas $P(A)P(B)=\\frac{1}{150}$.",
          "worked": "The event sets are\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\{15,30,45,60,75,90\\}\\\\B&=\\{15,25,35,45,55,65,75,85,95\\}\\\\A\\cap B&=\\{15,45,75\\}.\\end{align*}$$\nThere are $90$ equally likely outcomes.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A)&=\\frac{6}{90}\\\\P(A)&=\\frac{1}{15}\\\\P(B)&=\\frac{9}{90}\\\\P(B)&=\\frac{1}{10}\\\\P(A\\cap B)&=\\frac{3}{90}\\\\P(A\\cap B)&=\\frac{1}{30}\\\\P(A)P(B)&=\\frac{1}{15}\\times\\frac{1}{10}\\\\P(A)P(B)&=\\frac{1}{150}.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $P(A\\cap B)\\ne P(A)P(B)$, the events are dependent.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 124
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q17",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p39-q17-events",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\begin{aligned}A&=\\text{the number is divisible by 3}\\\\B&=\\text{the last digit is a multiple of 3}\\end{aligned}",
                  "display": true
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Independent events: $P(A\\cap B)=\\frac{2}{15}=P(A)P(B)$.",
          "worked": "There are $90$ equally likely outcomes, including $30$ multiples of $3$. The possible last digits for $B$ are $0,3,6,9$, each occurring nine times, so $B$ contains $36$ outcomes. For each of these four last digits, three numbers are divisible by $3$, so $A\\cap B$ contains $12$ outcomes.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A)&=\\frac{30}{90}\\\\P(A)&=\\frac{1}{3}\\\\P(B)&=\\frac{36}{90}\\\\P(B)&=\\frac{2}{5}\\\\P(A\\cap B)&=\\frac{12}{90}\\\\P(A\\cap B)&=\\frac{2}{15}\\\\P(A)P(B)&=\\frac{1}{3}\\times\\frac{2}{5}\\\\P(A)P(B)&=\\frac{2}{15}.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $P(A\\cap B)=P(A)P(B)$, the events are independent.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 116
      }
    ]
  },
